From b722c62f1e270edbd604a49ceaaf74e907278583 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:57:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] iommu/vsi: unwind prepared clocks when the interrupt is
 unavailable

vsi_iommu_probe() prepares every clock before it looks up the
interrupt. A devm_request_irq() failure unwinds them through
err_unprepare_clocks, but the platform_get_irq() failure immediately
before it returns directly, leaving the clocks prepared for as long as
the device exists.

Route that failure through the same unwind path.

Fixes: 917ace84b770 ("iommu: Add verisilicon IOMMU driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
index edb0c43087a26..8193fd62161fd 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
@@ -693,8 +693,10 @@ static int vsi_iommu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return err;
 
 	iommu->irq = platform_get_irq(pdev, 0);
-	if (iommu->irq < 0)
-		return iommu->irq;
+	if (iommu->irq < 0) {
+		err = iommu->irq;
+		goto err_unprepare_clocks;
+	}
 
 	err = devm_request_irq(iommu->dev, iommu->irq, vsi_iommu_irq,
 			       IRQF_SHARED, dev_name(dev), iommu);
